art runs from Oct 21, 2025 to Mar 2, 2026.","setup":"The stock rose about 57% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 11 weeks, peaking at $150.47 and pulling back 32% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jan 20, 2026 it closed at $105.78, below the base's floor of $106.21, without ever closing above the base high of $150.47. Volume that day was 23.5M shares, 1.06x the prior 10-day average. It kept sliding, down to $69.22, and the chart ends at $78.78.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakdown. The stock built what looked like a base, then broke out of the bottom instead of the top. There was never a breakout to buy. When a base gives way below, the move is to stay out, or get out fast if you bought early."}}